{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:24478-1","published":"2026-10-30T08:37:29Z","modified":"2026-11-04T17:23:18.634720440Z","related":["CVE-2026-59995","CVE-2026-59996","CVE-2026-59997","CVE-2026-59998","CVE-2026-59999","CVE-2026-60000","CVE-2026-60001","CVE-2026-60002"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-59995","CVE-2026-59996","CVE-2026-59997","CVE-2026-59998","CVE-2026-59999","CVE-2026-60000","CVE-2026-60001","CVE-2026-60002"],"summary":"Security update for openssh","details":"This update for openssh fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-59995: sftp: a malicious server could change the the location of downloaded files (bsc#1271044).\n- CVE-2026-59996: scp: a malicious server could write files to the parent directory of the intended target directory\n  (bsc#1271046).\n- CVE-2026-59997: sshd: internal-sftp command lines are silently truncated after the 9th argument (bsc#1271048).\n- CVE-2026-59998: sshd: Undocumented GSSAPIStrictAcceptorCheck behavior impacts security in Windows Active Directory\n  (bsc#1271049).\n- CVE-2026-59999: sshd: DisableForwarding=yes didn't override PermitTunnel=yes (bsc#1271052).\n- CVE-2026-60000: sshd: pre-authentication denial of service when GSSAPIAuthentication is enabled (bsc#1271053).\n- CVE-2026-60001: sshd: honor the minimum authentication delay (bsc#1271054).\n- CVE-2026-60002: ssh: client-side use-after-free when a server changes its host key during a key reexchange\n  (bsc#1271055).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"openssh","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Micro 6.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/openssh&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Micro%206.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.6p1-159998.2.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"openssh":"9.6p1-159998.2.1","openssh-clients":"9.6p1-159998.2.1","openssh-common":"9.6p1-159998.2.1","openssh-fips":"9.6p1-159998.2.1","openssh-server":"9.6p1-159998.2.1","openssh-server-config-rootlogin":"9.6p1-159998.2.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/